---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/templates/home.css';
---

<Layout
  title="The Cuts — Bez Ambar"
  description="The complete gallery of original Bez Ambar diamond cuts: Quadrillion® (Princess Cut), Blaze®, Divine Cut®, and the Elysian Cut™ family. Los Angeles, since 1979."
  canonical="https://bezambar.com/cuts"
  headerLight={true}
>

  <!-- ============================================================
       PAGE INTRO
       ============================================================ -->
  <div style="padding: clamp(100px, 14vw, 160px) 40px clamp(40px, 6vw, 80px); text-align: center; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <p class="segment__eyebrow">Bez Ambar</p>
    <h1 class="segment__title" style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4rem); margin-bottom: 24px;">The Cuts</h1>
    <p style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-soft);">Four original geometries. Four decades of invention. Each one a new argument about what light can do inside a stone.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       QUADRILLION® — THE PRINCESS CUT
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="segment" id="cut-quadrillion">
    <div class="segment__media segment__media--inset-square">
      <img
        src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_750/v1775786208/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Quadrillion_owciyv.jpg"
        srcset="https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_400/v1775786208/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Quadrillion_owciyv.jpg 400w,
                https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_750/v1775786208/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Quadrillion_owciyv.jpg 750w,
                https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_1100/v1775786208/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Quadrillion_owciyv.jpg 1100w"
        sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
        alt="The Quadrillion® cut — inventor of the Princess Cut, Bez Ambar"
        loading="eager">
    </div>
    <div class="segment__content">
      <p class="segment__eyebrow">1982 &middot; Patented &middot; DeBeers Award</p>
      <h2 class="segment__title">Quadrillion® — The Princess Cut</h2>
      <p class="segment__body">A square brilliant with chevron facets that direct light inward and back up through the table. The trade adopted it immediately. The world eventually called it the Princess cut &mdash; Bez&rsquo;s cut, under a different name. It became the most popular diamond shape on Earth. The man who invented it kept working.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       BLAZE®
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="segment segment--reverse" id="cut-blaze">
    <div class="segment__media segment__media--inset-square" style="background: #e8e4df; min-height: 400px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
      <p style="color: #aaa; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.1em;">IMAGE PLACEHOLDER</p>
    </div>
    <div class="segment__content">
      <p class="segment__eyebrow">Patented &middot; Registered Trademark</p>
      <h2 class="segment__title">Blaze®</h2>
      <p class="segment__body">Thirteen precisely aligned facets produce a starburst of light visible to the naked eye under white light. This effect is specific to the Blaze® geometry &mdash; it cannot be replicated by any other arrangement of facets. No other house in the world produces it. The starburst is not a coincidence of polish. It is the result.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       DIVINE CUT®
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="segment" id="cut-divine">
    <div class="segment__media segment__media--inset-square" style="background: #e8e4df; min-height: 400px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;">
      <p style="color: #aaa; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.1em;">IMAGE PLACEHOLDER</p>
    </div>
    <div class="segment__content">
      <p class="segment__eyebrow">Patented &middot; Registered Trademark</p>
      <h2 class="segment__title">Divine Cut®</h2>
      <p class="segment__body">A round brilliant engineered for a specific quality of dispersion &mdash; the way white light separates into color inside a well-cut stone. Continuing forty years of study into how light moves, the Divine Cut® is Bez Ambar&rsquo;s answer to the round brilliant, reengineered from first principles.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       ELYSIAN CUT™ — A FAMILY OF SEVEN
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="segment segment--reverse" id="cut-elysian">
    <div class="segment__media segment__media--inset-square">
      <img
        src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_750/v1779074065/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Elysian_cut_oval_qcdt5r.jpg"
        srcset="https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_400/v1779074065/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Elysian_cut_oval_qcdt5r.jpg 400w,
                https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_750/v1779074065/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Elysian_cut_oval_qcdt5r.jpg 750w,
                https://res.cloudinary.com/dlg2mou53/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,w_1100/v1779074065/Jewelry%20Images/Stones/Elysian_cut_oval_qcdt5r.jpg 1100w"
        sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw"
        alt="The Elysian Cut™ Oval — one of seven original step-cut geometries by Bez Ambar"
        loading="lazy">
    </div>
    <div class="segment__content">
      <p class="segment__eyebrow">Seven Shapes &middot; Registered Trademark</p>
      <h2 class="segment__title">Elysian Cut™</h2>
      <p class="segment__body">Not a single shape &mdash; a system. Seven original step-cut geometries, each engineered from the stone outward. The line of the crown. The relationship of the pavilion. The angles that decide whether light becomes a flicker or a continuous line. Pear. Oval. Marquise. Emerald. Octagon. Hex. Triangle.</p>
      <a href="/elysian-cut" class="segment__cta">Discover the Full Family</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       HERITAGE CLOSING
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="heritage">
    <p class="heritage__quote">&ldquo;The cutter doesn&rsquo;t shape the stone. He sculpts the light inside it.&rdquo;</p>
    <p class="heritage__attribution">&mdash; Bez Ambar</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       DESIGNER TEXT — faceting philosophy
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="segment segment--centered" id="segment-designer">
    <div class="segment__content segment__content--wide">
      <p class="segment__body">To cut a diamond is to chisel light. The stone is the medium. Fire, scintillation, and brilliance &mdash; the three ways light behaves inside a well-cut stone &mdash; are the result. Every facet is a decision about where light will land, where it will bend, where it will return to the eye.</p>
      <p class="segment__body">Bez Ambar has spent fifty years doing exactly that. Drawing geometries where none existed &mdash; the modern Princess, the Blaze&reg;, the Elysian&trade;, and many original custom cuts. Each is an original argument about how a stone should behave under a lamp: where it should hold colour, where it should flash, where it should keep quiet.</p>
      <p class="segment__body">Faceting is not decoration. It is sculpture. And the material is always light.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
